<section id="presentation">
    <div class="section-label">In her own words</div>
    <h2>Meet <em>Chelsey</em></h2>
    <div class="video-wrapper fade-up">
        <video src="presentation.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls></video>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="about">
    <div class="about-left fade-up">
        <div class="about-portrait">
            <div class="about-portrait-fill">
                <span class="portrait-initials">CS</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-right">
        <div class="section-label">About me</div>
        <h2>Nurse first.<br /><em>Engineer</em> now.</h2>
        <br /><br />
        <p>
            I spent years as an ICU RN &mdash; managing vents, drips, and deteriorating patients &mdash; and learned
            firsthand that bad software costs more than time. It costs patient safety. That experience
            is the reason I write code.
        </p>
        <p>
            Transitioning into health tech engineering means I bring something most developers don&rsquo;t have:
            I&rsquo;ve sat at the workstation at 3am trying to find a lab value in six clicks when one would do.
            I know what clinical workflows actually look like, and I build accordingly.
        </p>
        <p>
            My target is companies like <strong>Epic, Oracle Health, Meditech, or AWS HealthLake</strong> &mdash;
            places where clinical domain expertise and software engineering ability compound each other.
            Right now I&rsquo;m building that foundation through <strong>EpicPetEMR</strong>, a full EMR system
            in Blazor/.NET, and getting deep into AWS cloud architecture.
        </p>
        <p>
            Based in West Virginia with my partner Luke, a rotating cast of dogs, and a strong opinion
            about how EMR UI should actually work.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="skills">
    <div class="section-label">What I work with</div>
    <h2>Skills &amp; <em>Domain Expertise</em></h2>
    <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-card fade-up">
            <div class="skill-card-num">01</div>
            <h3>Clinical Domain Knowledge</h3>
            <p>Years as an ICU nurse give me fluency in clinical workflows, patient data models,
            order entry, documentation burden, and the places EHR systems fail nurses and
            physicians daily. I build software that reflects how care actually happens.</p>
            <div class="skill-tags">
                <span class="skill-tag">Critical Care</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">ICU Workflows</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">Clinical Documentation</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">Patient Safety</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">EHR UX</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card fade-up">
            <div class="skill-card-num">02</div>
            <h3>Health Tech Engineering</h3>
            <p>Building EMR-style systems from scratch in Blazor and .NET. Familiar with HL7/FHIR
            data standards, clinical data modeling, and the access control patterns that
            healthcare software demands.</p>
            <div class="skill-tags">
                <span class="skill-tag">C# / .NET</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">Blazor WASM</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">FHIR / HL7</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">REST APIs</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">JWT Auth</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-card fade-up">
            <div class="skill-card-num">03</div>
            <h3>Cloud Infrastructure</h3>
            <p>Learning AWS with a focus on healthcare-relevant services &mdash; HIPAA-eligible
            infrastructure, cloud storage, serverless compute, and the architectural patterns
            that underpin platforms like Epic on AWS.</p>
            <div class="skill-tags">
                <span class="skill-tag">AWS</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">IAM</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">EC2 / S3</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">Lambda</span>
                <span class="skill-tag">HealthLake</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

